1
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:10,800
Years ago, I took a trip to Egypt,
where I met an old hag named Anyaba.

2
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:14,280
She told me to fire this
arrow at whoever it desired.

3
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:17,080
For the Impaled would become my ally.

4
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:18,992
After the initial shock,

5
00:00:19,080 --> 00:00:23,377
they would witness a unique power rising
up from the deep recesses of their souls.

6
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:26,717
If memory serves, she
referred to them as Stans.

7
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:28,277
Jotaro Kujo.

8
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:33,140
If he and his minion army of Hitman
are pursuing my dear Yoshikage,

9
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:35,676
then I'll have to create my own army.

10
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:36,980
One like no other.

11
00:00:37,260 --> 00:00:38,920
An army of stand users.

12
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:40,740
Here we are, Arrow.

13
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:43,157
The time's come to select your prey.

14
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:45,880
Which of these vessels do you desire? Huh?

15
00:00:48,360 --> 00:00:49,900
A telephone pole?

16
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:52,004
Why would you want a Dolphin?

17
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:54,320
Wait a minute.

18
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:56,440
You desire that child?

19
00:00:57,920 --> 00:01:01,980
So you're telling me a child is to
become the first of my new allies?

20
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:08,700
If that is your will, I'll pierce the
lad's soul and add him to our ranks!

21
00:01:40,580 --> 00:01:41,897
Thank

22
00:01:41,980 --> 00:01:43,297
you

23
00:01:43,380 --> 00:01:50,380
so

24
00:01:51,520 --> 00:01:56,517
much for watching. I'm chasing you!

25
00:01:56,600 --> 00:02:00,860
I'm chasing you!

26
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:05,737
I can't walk by the road, go
chase you! I'm chasing you!

27
00:02:05,820 --> 00:02:09,640
If I'm chasing you, I'll get you ready!

28
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:15,780
I'll get your chance to get
by the end of the story.

29
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:18,460
I'm chasing you!

30
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:41,960
Well, if it isn't our manga
artist extraordinaire.

31
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:44,692
I hope you're having a good morning, sir.

32
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:47,180
Hmm, snapping a few photos, eh?

33
00:02:47,760 --> 00:02:52,097
I'm trying to take candid shots of office
workers while on their morning commute.

34
00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:53,010
Oh?

35
00:02:53,093 --> 00:02:54,196
Just think about it.

36
00:02:54,300 --> 00:02:57,418
Yoshikage Kira, he stole
someone's identity, correct?

37
00:02:57,860 --> 00:03:02,620
Well, he's probably commuting to work
just as his victim once did. You think?

38
00:03:03,420 --> 00:03:07,120
He's between 25 and 35
and nearly 2 meters tall.

39
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:11,597
Add in that he's an office worker and
our suspect pool dramatically decreases.

40
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:12,560
I see.

41
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:15,897
But how can you be sure he
uses this exact station?

42
00:03:15,980 --> 00:03:18,740
He could just as easily commute by car.

43
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:20,320
That could be the case.

44
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:23,072
But, though he may have changed his face,

45
00:03:23,180 --> 00:03:26,377
it's very likely that he will
still fall into old habits.

46
00:03:26,460 --> 00:03:27,290
Habits.

47
00:03:27,373 --> 00:03:29,897
That'll arouse the suspicion
of his cover family.

48
00:03:29,980 --> 00:03:32,509
By now they must realize
something's amiss.

49
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:34,030
Hmm.

50
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:38,457
My biggest fear is that the family
will recognize their intruder,

51
00:03:38,540 --> 00:03:40,837
prompting him to eliminate them as well.

52
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:43,537
And don't you think for a
moment that I'm going soft?

53
00:03:43,620 --> 00:03:46,738
I just want to find Kira
before he wreaks more havoc.

54
00:03:48,140 --> 00:03:49,860
Hey, tall bros!

55
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:56,214
Does one of you want to play
me in a game of Rochambeau?

56
00:03:57,080 --> 00:03:57,910
Rocham!

57
00:03:58,280 --> 00:04:00,137
What are you two, deaf or something?

58
00:04:00,220 --> 00:04:01,050
Play with me!

59
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:03,497
What an oddball. Just play already!

60
00:04:03,580 --> 00:04:07,109
I suppose every station has a
nut job or two running around.

61
00:04:07,300 --> 00:04:08,130
Well, Mr.

62
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:11,657
Joestar, if you come across any
leads, you know how to reach me.

63
00:04:11,740 --> 00:04:15,505
Don't go sticking your nose in
trouble all by your lonesome now.

64
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:21,220
Hey, mister!

65
00:04:21,480 --> 00:04:23,186
Aren't you that manga artist?

66
00:04:24,540 --> 00:04:26,977
You stopped drawing for
a little while, right?

67
00:04:27,060 --> 00:04:29,920
I'm a big Shonen Jump
fan, so I know your work!

68
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:31,140
Now how about it?

69
00:04:31,320 --> 00:04:33,817
It won't kill you to
play with me, will it?

70
00:04:33,900 --> 00:04:35,520
What is your problem, kid?

71
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:36,590
Hit the bricks!

72
00:04:36,673 --> 00:04:39,040
But I just want to play Rochambeau.

73
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:40,180
It'll be fun!

74
00:04:44,620 --> 00:04:45,617
What the...

75
00:04:45,700 --> 00:04:46,720
how peculiar.

76
00:04:47,020 --> 00:04:49,560
The boy's left cheek has a big hole in it.

77
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:52,406
It's so deep, I bet it
extends into his mouth.

78
00:04:52,660 --> 00:04:54,957
No hard feelings if you win, but...

79
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:56,680
A try we go again.

80
00:04:56,940 --> 00:05:00,120
If you're late, then you
lose, understand? Ready?

81
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:01,820
And Rocham!

82
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:04,540
This kid is being weirdly tenacious.

83
00:05:05,420 --> 00:05:07,340
Is he a stand user?

84
00:05:10,620 --> 00:05:12,240
All right then!

85
00:05:12,540 --> 00:05:13,600
Road ship!

86
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:15,480
Heaven's door!

87
00:05:15,660 --> 00:05:16,760
Shut this brat up!

88
00:05:29,220 --> 00:05:31,080
Hmm, now let's see.

89
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:34,320
It says his name is Ken Oyunagi, age 11.

90
00:05:34,820 --> 00:05:37,702
I'm not seeing anything
about him having a stand.

91
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:41,120
He got the injury when he
fell from a telephone pole.

92
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:44,580
Hmm, interesting.

93
00:05:45,840 --> 00:05:48,075
He feels compelled to play Rochambeau.

94
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:49,070
Bizarre, but...

95
00:05:49,153 --> 00:05:51,297
Are you two gentlemen
gonna need a ride or what?

96
00:05:51,380 --> 00:05:53,792
Could we trouble you for 30 more seconds?

97
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:57,310
Fire away!

98
00:05:57,393 --> 00:05:59,908
Once we do this, you'll
have to leave me be.

99
00:06:01,220 --> 00:06:02,050
Rochambeau!

100
00:06:04,420 --> 00:06:05,640
Well, so long.

101
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:09,580
How could I lose?

102
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:21,840
I suppose I've done enough
work for one day. Yo!

103
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:23,180
Rohan Sensei!

104
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:25,297
Are you calling it quits for the day?

105
00:06:25,380 --> 00:06:28,792
Instead of sitting all by
yourself, why don't you join us?

106
00:06:29,460 --> 00:06:30,290
Perfect.

107
00:06:30,373 --> 00:06:33,400
A self-absorbed jerk-off,
a moron, and a bitch.

108
00:06:33,900 --> 00:06:37,076
Three people I have absolutely
nothing in common with.

109
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:40,060
Hey guys, sorry I'm working at the moment.

110
00:06:40,320 --> 00:06:41,440
Maybe another time.

111
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:42,820
Oh, gotcha.

112
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:44,230
Huh?

113
00:06:45,220 --> 00:06:46,620
Hey, you brat!

114
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:47,837
What do you think you're doing?

115
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:49,391
I was going to sit there.

116
00:06:50,180 --> 00:06:52,800
I bet, but you never actually sat down.

117
00:06:53,140 --> 00:06:54,977
The seat was free, so I took it.

118
00:06:55,060 --> 00:06:57,589
You snooze, you lose,
you know what I mean?

119
00:06:58,220 --> 00:06:59,460
I have had enough.

120
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:00,739
What is your deal?

121
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:03,377
Let's settle this with Rochambeau.

122
00:07:03,460 --> 00:07:04,977
Winner takes the seat, okay?

123
00:07:05,060 --> 00:07:05,890
Again?

124
00:07:05,973 --> 00:07:06,803
Oh, man!

125
00:07:08,340 --> 00:07:09,170
AHH!

126
00:07:09,840 --> 00:07:10,720
Not fair!

127
00:07:10,960 --> 00:07:13,254
I sat here first, so you can't have it!

128
00:07:13,580 --> 00:07:15,157
This is my senior baby!

129
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:16,417
Is there a problem here?

130
00:07:16,500 --> 00:07:17,500
Everywhere, fine.

131
00:07:17,620 --> 00:07:20,340
Rohan-sensei, why can't
you give him a break?

132
00:07:20,620 --> 00:07:21,637
Come on, look at him.

133
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:22,661
He's just a kid.

134
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:24,018
Yeah, I'm with him.

135
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:25,957
You're supposed to be the mature one.

136
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:27,457
You could try sitting next to him.

137
00:07:27,540 --> 00:07:28,370
Shut up!

138
00:07:28,453 --> 00:07:29,692
None of you are helping!

139
00:07:30,260 --> 00:07:31,090
Fine, kid.

140
00:07:31,260 --> 00:07:32,697
I'll play with you again.

141
00:07:32,780 --> 00:07:35,192
Well, that's what you're after, isn't it?

142
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:37,860
Yeah, that's more like it!

143
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:39,860
Okay, now get ready!

144
00:07:41,780 --> 00:07:43,520
Ro-Cham-Bo!

145
00:07:45,580 --> 00:07:47,117
Well, would you look at that!

146
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:48,082
I'm the winner!

147
00:07:49,180 --> 00:07:50,460
Got nothing to say?

148
00:07:50,640 --> 00:07:54,577
I, for one, have never been so happy
to win a game of Ro-Cham-Bo in my life!

149
00:07:54,660 --> 00:07:56,500
You call this being mature?

150
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:02,176
There's no better feeling than
destroying a smug whelp in his own game.

151
00:08:05,500 --> 00:08:07,180
Damn, must again!

152
00:08:13,820 --> 00:08:14,650
Oh...

153
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:17,760
This is some good material.

154
00:08:18,140 --> 00:08:21,320
Who knew such an obscure
book could be found in Mario?

155
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:23,280
Hmm, 7,500 yen.

156
00:08:23,520 --> 00:08:25,000
Do I have that much?

157
00:08:26,860 --> 00:08:29,400
Excuse me, I want to buy this book!

158
00:08:29,860 --> 00:08:31,880
You obnoxious little...

159
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:36,080
Let's duke it out Ro-Sham-Beau-Style!

160
00:08:36,860 --> 00:08:37,690
Fine.

161
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,020
Brace yourself!

162
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:40,820
Ro-Sham!

163
00:08:41,720 --> 00:08:42,550
Rock!

164
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:46,769
You're messing with
the wrong artist, punk!

165
00:08:48,420 --> 00:08:50,320
Look at that! I won!

166
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:52,427
Still think I'm just a punk?

167
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:56,240
One win, two losses!

168
00:08:56,700 --> 00:08:58,524
What the hell is going on here?

169
00:09:01,740 --> 00:09:03,840
Uh, what is this?

170
00:09:05,040 --> 00:09:06,240
What the...

171
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:08,780
It's that damn cheek hole!

172
00:09:09,080 --> 00:09:13,180
So I wasn't off base before,
you might be a user! What?

173
00:09:14,520 --> 00:09:16,140
This is freaking awesome!

174
00:09:16,420 --> 00:09:19,237
I never would have guessed it
was hiding something so cool!

175
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:22,617
I've never felt anything like the
energy flowing into me right now!

176
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:23,917
It's totally awesome!

177
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,706
It's like being supercharged!

178
00:09:25,860 --> 00:09:26,700
That's enough!

179
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:30,547
Now quickly, heaven's door, turn
this little brat into a book!

180
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:41,326
Judging from his sloppy work,

181
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:44,675
that must have been the first
time he's used his stand.

182
00:09:44,900 --> 00:09:48,253
However, that doesn't mean he
won't master it given time.

183
00:09:50,500 --> 00:09:53,860
I want to beat the crap out
of Rohan and Rochambeau, huh?

184
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:56,857
Rochambeau isn't a game of chance.

185
00:09:56,940 --> 00:09:59,160
It's a psychological game of will.

186
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:03,191
If I beat Rohan at Rochambeau,
it means I've outwilled him.

187
00:10:03,660 --> 00:10:07,307
Rohan's only 20 years old, but
he lives life on his own terms.

188
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:10,340
His work also inspires
a whole lot of people.

189
00:10:10,660 --> 00:10:13,960
If I can beat the crap out
of Rohan in Rochambeau,

190
00:10:14,060 --> 00:10:16,637
that'll prove I can be
better than him one day.

191
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:21,602
I can't wait to grow up, because then I'll
be just as respected as the great Rohan.

192
00:10:24,060 --> 00:10:25,120
I knew it!

193
00:10:25,340 --> 00:10:28,277
This kid is well on the road
to becoming a stand user.

194
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:30,557
The arrow must have just pierced his soul

195
00:10:30,640 --> 00:10:33,797
ability winning in Rochambeau
makes my opponent's

196
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:36,937
energy my own But I must play five games

197
00:10:37,020 --> 00:10:39,617
winning two games only
gives me partial energy,

198
00:10:39,700 --> 00:10:41,580
so he needs to win five

199
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:54,580
It can't be how did you so this powers
called a stand that's pretty awesome

200
00:10:55,480 --> 00:10:58,077
Thought you dodged a
bullet there, didn't ya?

201
00:10:58,160 --> 00:11:02,557
Well, think again, because I've already
got a third of your so-called stand!

202
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:03,470
What?

203
00:11:03,553 --> 00:11:04,920
My right arm is gone!

204
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:09,358
It sure is, and one third of its
incredible power is under my control!

205
00:11:11,380 --> 00:11:14,640
That means you can't poke
around in my head anymore!

206
00:11:15,220 --> 00:11:16,050
Damn you!

207
00:11:16,460 --> 00:11:20,600
Oh, and if I win two more times,
all of your powers will be mine!

208
00:11:21,260 --> 00:11:22,940
You punk, dammit!

209
00:11:23,180 --> 00:11:24,945
You won't get away with this?!

210
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:30,317
Taking a swing at me like
that was pretty ballsy.

211
00:11:30,400 --> 00:11:32,929
Guess you got a taste
of your own medicine!

212
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:34,420
Okay, now I get it.

213
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:37,337
I have to defeat you in
another game of Rochambeau.

214
00:11:37,420 --> 00:11:40,596
That's the only way I'll win
back my Stan's right arm.

215
00:11:41,900 --> 00:11:42,730
Game on!

216
00:11:42,940 --> 00:11:43,960
Here we go!

217
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:55,017
Are you completely oblivious
to the plight you're in?

218
00:11:55,100 --> 00:11:57,717
If you lose just one more
time, you're finished.

219
00:11:57,800 --> 00:12:00,517
Surely by now you've realized
you're all out of chances.

220
00:12:00,600 --> 00:12:03,797
Since I know you're a stand
user, I'll show you no mercy.

221
00:12:03,880 --> 00:12:07,397
The moment I retrieve my right arm,
I'm putting you out of commission.

222
00:12:07,480 --> 00:12:08,360
Admit defeat!

223
00:12:08,660 --> 00:12:10,836
Wait, are you trying to psych me out?

224
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:12,862
Alright, let's get this started.

225
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:15,220
I'm not ready to play just yet.

226
00:12:15,420 --> 00:12:17,437
I won the last match using paper.

227
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:21,597
So I guess it's only natural to want
to go with rock or scissors this time.

228
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:24,537
But it'd be kind of stupid to go
with the obvious just cause...

229
00:12:24,620 --> 00:12:29,017
And it's pretty clear to anyone with eyes
you're not the naive type, Rohan-sensei.

230
00:12:29,100 --> 00:12:31,777
So maybe going with paper
would be the best way to go.

231
00:12:31,860 --> 00:12:33,860
I mean, what could it hurt, right?

232
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:35,828
Okay, I've made up my mind!

233
00:12:36,600 --> 00:12:37,430
Let's go!

234
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:40,260
Ro-sham-fo!

235
00:12:41,560 --> 00:12:42,390
What?

236
00:12:42,473 --> 00:12:43,303
I did it!

237
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:46,322
I outwilled Rohan-sensei
with the power of paper!

238
00:12:47,520 --> 00:12:49,579
That makes two wins and two losses.

239
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:51,020
Sucks for you.

240
00:13:08,580 --> 00:13:11,377
I just took the lower
half of your heavens door.

241
00:13:11,460 --> 00:13:14,117
If you're tired, you could
rest on that bench over there.

242
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:16,317
No, that won't be necessary.

243
00:13:16,400 --> 00:13:18,360
When vanquishing your opponent,

244
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:23,260
you must savor it and look down on
the Concord with pity and disdain.

245
00:13:25,260 --> 00:13:29,820
I've got two wins and two losses, so
we're both one game away from destiny.

246
00:13:30,160 --> 00:13:33,440
But I'm so close to victory,
I can almost taste it!

247
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:37,500
I know I lost twice, but I came
back and won twice in a row!

248
00:13:37,740 --> 00:13:39,677
It's the other way around for you!

249
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:40,840
You've lost twice!

250
00:13:41,180 --> 00:13:44,474
You're smack dab in the middle
of a major losing streak!

251
00:13:50,980 --> 00:13:51,810
Marvelous!

252
00:13:51,893 --> 00:13:55,520
As expected from one chosen by
the arrow, we're almost there.

253
00:13:55,860 --> 00:13:59,817
If this kid can finish absorbing
Rohan Kishibe's mind-reading powers,

254
00:13:59,900 --> 00:14:01,135
we'll be unstoppable.

255
00:14:01,260 --> 00:14:04,220
You'll serve my precious Yoshikage well.

256
00:14:04,740 --> 00:14:05,660
Good work.

257
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:08,037
You've gotten better at the mind games.

258
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:10,002
Quite impressive for a punk kid.

259
00:14:10,180 --> 00:14:13,300
You've lost the game twice
in a row. That's a fact!

260
00:14:13,980 --> 00:14:15,039
Yes, you're right.

261
00:14:15,280 --> 00:14:16,320
I won't argue.

262
00:14:16,860 --> 00:14:20,897
Since you're big on facts, I take it
you won't mind if I tell you another.

263
00:14:20,980 --> 00:14:24,580
I'm positive you won't be
using paper for this duel.

264
00:14:26,860 --> 00:14:28,420
Guess we'll find out, huh?

265
00:14:28,540 --> 00:14:29,617
Let's not get ahead of ourselves.

266
00:14:29,700 --> 00:14:30,935
I'm not finished yet.

267
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:33,997
I went with Rock twice,
and it cost me both times.

268
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:37,800
It's obvious now that Rock is
my unlucky play. Am I wrong?

269
00:14:38,260 --> 00:14:43,142
It goes without saying I'd be adverse to
using Rock again when it's been so unkind.

270
00:14:43,300 --> 00:14:47,837
And since I won't be going with rock this
time, you won't be able to use paper.

271
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:51,077
Using it would be the same as
admitting I'm not on a losing streak,

272
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:52,837
despite what you said a while back.

273
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:53,750
Ha!

274
00:14:53,833 --> 00:14:54,952
You're still gonna lose!

275
00:14:57,160 --> 00:14:59,000
All right, let's do this!

276
00:14:59,880 --> 00:15:00,780
It's time!

277
00:15:01,320 --> 00:15:03,200
Rope! Shamp! Rope!

278
00:15:05,020 --> 00:15:07,760
Oh, that bluffing, and
he still used paper.

279
00:15:08,060 --> 00:15:09,460
What mental fortitude!

280
00:15:09,780 --> 00:15:11,477
There's no way I'm gonna lose to him.

281
00:15:11,560 --> 00:15:13,957
I still have the upper hand in this match.

282
00:15:14,040 --> 00:15:16,100
I'll use paper four times in a row.

283
00:15:16,280 --> 00:15:17,537
This game's in the bag!

284
00:15:17,620 --> 00:15:19,160
Time to go back to rock.

285
00:15:19,400 --> 00:15:21,635
I'll make misfortune work in my favor.

286
00:15:21,860 --> 00:15:23,000
Here we go!

287
00:15:27,660 --> 00:15:29,248
What's wrong with my knees?

288
00:15:30,740 --> 00:15:31,570
Huh?

289
00:15:31,653 --> 00:15:33,460
He's never moved like that before!

290
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:37,120
The only move Rohan hasn't
used yet is scissors. Crap!

291
00:15:37,340 --> 00:15:40,046
Going with paper four
times in a row is risky!

292
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:42,740
What? No way!

293
00:15:42,840 --> 00:15:45,134
It seems Rock wasn't unlucky after all.

294
00:15:48,700 --> 00:15:50,440
That bastard! Huh?

295
00:15:50,820 --> 00:15:52,340
No, that's not good!

296
00:15:56,560 --> 00:15:58,600
Hey, mister, can I talk to you?

297
00:15:58,920 --> 00:16:02,580
So, Rohan-sensei, those two
are probably users too, right?

298
00:16:03,300 --> 00:16:05,829
Yeah, I'm right, I can
feel it in my bones.

299
00:16:06,160 --> 00:16:07,460
Let's test my luck.

300
00:16:07,640 --> 00:16:10,857
If it all runs out, those two will
head over here and rescue you.

301
00:16:10,940 --> 00:16:15,397
But if luck is on my side coming over here
will be the last thing on their minds.

302
00:16:15,480 --> 00:16:17,397
Oh, look at that It's Rohan again.

303
00:16:17,480 --> 00:16:19,560
I really can't stand that guy

304
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:22,637
Let's just smile at him and keep walking.

305
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:25,760
Well, I suppose we could do that

306
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:29,820
Their child is

307
00:16:30,900 --> 00:16:33,000
Yes, he has to be

308
00:16:34,380 --> 00:16:36,720
One of Rohan's adoring fans.

309
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:38,320
See you again soon.

310
00:16:38,680 --> 00:16:40,000
Yeah later, man

311
00:16:42,120 --> 00:16:43,437
Well, what do you know?

312
00:16:43,520 --> 00:16:46,200
Seems luck is still on
my side, Rohan-sensei.

313
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:47,740
So are you scared yet?

314
00:16:49,020 --> 00:16:51,337
I've never felt more
confident about winning!

315
00:16:51,420 --> 00:16:53,714
As long as I've got luck, I can't lose!

316
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:56,717
I feel like I could play a high-stakes
game of Russian Roulette with

317
00:16:56,800 --> 00:17:01,271
five out of six bullets in the chamber
and still live to tell the epic tale!

318
00:17:02,080 --> 00:17:04,433
Even a shower of glass is nothing to me!

319
00:17:18,340 --> 00:17:20,417
Now then, it's time for the final match.

320
00:17:20,500 --> 00:17:22,441
Who's going to win, Rohan-sensei?

321
00:17:27,320 --> 00:17:28,917
What the heck are you doing?

322
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:31,017
Hurry and assume your Rochambeau pose.

323
00:17:31,100 --> 00:17:32,137
It's time to play.

324
00:17:32,220 --> 00:17:34,857
You're the one who needs to
hurry up and get started.

325
00:17:34,940 --> 00:17:36,180
I made my move.

326
00:17:36,320 --> 00:17:37,460
You just missed it.

327
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:39,720
You can knock off the jokes, okay?

328
00:17:39,900 --> 00:17:40,841
It's not a joke.

329
00:17:40,940 --> 00:17:44,060
Well, you said your aim is to surpass me.

330
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:47,887
But since I'm a bit older, I'll
let you in on a little secret.

331
00:17:48,040 --> 00:17:52,117
Beating one's opponent isn't all that
difficult when you think about it.

332
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:54,337
What's really challenging is...

333
00:17:54,420 --> 00:17:55,479
And pay attention.

334
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:59,800
The real challenge is
truly outdoing oneself,

335
00:18:00,140 --> 00:18:02,964
which is what I'm going
to do using my own luck.

336
00:18:10,120 --> 00:18:11,600
Let's go, Rohan!

337
00:18:11,920 --> 00:18:13,120
Time to play!

338
00:18:13,620 --> 00:18:14,720
Oh, chef!

339
00:18:16,280 --> 00:18:17,460
There we go!

340
00:18:17,700 --> 00:18:18,935
How do you like that?

341
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:24,060
Wait, what's going on? What?

342
00:18:27,740 --> 00:18:28,880
What happened?

343
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:31,906
Why am I all of a sudden
making the rock move?

344
00:18:34,060 --> 00:18:36,340
That makes three wins and two losses.

345
00:18:36,600 --> 00:18:38,482
Now you've got the unlucky rock.

346
00:18:38,660 --> 00:18:39,897
I couldn't see it before,

347
00:18:39,980 --> 00:18:43,980
but it wasn't just Joseph Joestar
who paid me a visit, luck did too.

348
00:18:44,240 --> 00:18:45,760
The invisible baby.

349
00:18:51,280 --> 00:18:53,997
You put too much energy
into being given luck

350
00:18:54,080 --> 00:18:56,700
while I took it upon
myself to make my own.

351
00:18:56,940 --> 00:18:59,820
That is the very meaning
of outdoing oneself.

352
00:19:03,960 --> 00:19:07,940
Now then, as I recall, I promise
to put you out of commission.

353
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:13,800
I'm going to write, as long as I
live, I shall lose it, Rochambeau.

354
00:19:14,140 --> 00:19:16,600
And my stand shall be no more, fiend.

355
00:19:18,340 --> 00:19:19,400
Just shut up!

356
00:19:19,660 --> 00:19:21,360
Stay away from me, Rohan!

357
00:19:22,780 --> 00:19:26,180
I swear, if you touch
me, the baby gets it!

358
00:19:27,120 --> 00:19:28,020
You fool!

359
00:19:28,220 --> 00:19:30,857
Do you have any idea
what it is you're doing?

360
00:19:30,940 --> 00:19:33,180
We've moved on now to a war of words!

361
